Looking at the shape, the dot sits in the middle-left region. Working out the tiling: the 4-square bar (B) must fill the top row, the corner piece (A) fits the bottom-right, and the stair-shaped piece (E) slides into the middle so that one of its squares lands exactly on the dotted cell (with the step of the staircase running along the dashed diagonal shown). The remaining pieces (C and D) then fill the left and bottom portions.

Thus the piece lying on the dot is the staircase piece E.

\boxed{E}
